th  saith them at all  he was tired of being weak all those  dreams he had of being a hero  were they all just delusions was he  fated to be weak for the rest of his  life  something inside of side them are  triggers he runs after the monster  desperately trying to get his 200 yen  back  it wasn't that he didn't want to lose  his 200 yen it wasn't that it was more  like he didn't want to just sit by as  someone  or something took his money he didn't  want to be weak  he changed the monster for a while but  at one point the monster just turned and  bumped right into him  saitama was out for an hour when he woke  up the monster was already dealt with  in the end he never got his 200 yen back  and the teacher lectured him  once again more so than before and then  as he's on his way back home  saitama's mind is full of thoughts his  monologue clearly represented the  current state of his existence  he says that he might not be fit to live  in this society he doesn't have the  faintest idea of how to live in this  world  all he ever does is lose will he ever be  able to live his life properly when he's  this weak  these were the thoughts that lurked  around in the mind of the 12 year old  saitama  fast forward 10 years later we see a bit  of the day saitama became a hero for the  first time  this flashback is shown in the very  first episode  saitama is a 22 year old unemployed man  he's hunting for a job but with no luck  all he's doing is working part-time at a  convenience store but then one day after  coming back from another failed  interview  he encounters a monster called crablante  however when the crab sees the look  inside them as eyes  he decides to spare him maybe it's  because the crab  somehow related to saitama's lifeless  eyes so he spares him and goes back to  find the boy with a cleft like a chin  cytoma doesn't think much of it but he  does see the child before the crab  and a few moments later the crabs also  there  now as the man who once saw out to 